/**
 * @defgroup Radiation Neutrino M1 Radiation Gem
 *
 * The Radiation contribution documented here is a grey, one-group,
 * three-species neutrino M1 surface. It provides transported number and
 * energy/momentum moments, symmetric Rusanov transport, realizability repair,
 * explicit source helpers, lepton-number exchange, and a frozen-rate local
 * implicit update.
 *
 * The neutrino operators consume provider-supplied
 * @c ghl_m1_neutrino_rates. The provider owns EOS lookup, unit conversion,
 * weak-rate channel selection, equilibrium targets, and the production
 * microphysics boundary. The installed public surface is declared in
 * @ref ghl_m1.h, @ref ghl_neutrino_rate_provider.h, and
 * @ref ghl_nrpyleakage.h.
 *
 * Electron-flavor pair, plasmon, and bremsstrahlung emissivities are stored
 * separately in @c ghl_m1_neutrino_rates::eta_N_pair and
 * @c ghl_m1_neutrino_rates::eta_E_pair. Use
 * @ref ghl_m1_solve_neutrino_pair_source_update for the two electron species
 * together. It includes the independent charged-current/scattering update
 * and the grey paired collision update, conserving the pair number difference
 * and publishing both species atomically. Single-species source operations
 * reject electron pair rates. The equations and approximation are documented
 * in @c GRHayL/Radiation/PAIR_SOURCE_MODEL.md.
 * The closure enforces the radiation trace at zero flux, using its flagged
 * Eulerian admissibility fallback when necessary. The neutrino Newton solve
 * can use an admissible source predictor at an exact-zero-flux start without
 * changing the source base or residual equation.
 *
 * The deterministic, table-free provider is initialized by
 * @ref ghl_neutrino_rate_provider_initialize_default; the table-backed
 * provider path is initialized by
 * @ref ghl_neutrino_rate_provider_initialize_nrpyleakage. A caller initializes
 * its cache with @ref ghl_neutrino_rate_provider_cache_initialize and may
 * zero-initialize its diagnostics with
 * @c ghl_neutrino_rate_provider_diagnostics diagnostics = {0}. The caller
 * increments @c eos_generation after mutating an EOS/table object in place so
 * cache reuse and hold-last recovery cannot cross a changed table state.
 *
 * HDF5 is a build-time dependency of tabulated EOS lookup, not of the public
 * header aggregate. In a @c GHL_DISABLE_HDF5 build the headers remain
 * includable and the production provider returns
 * @c ghl_error_used_disabled_hdf5 without publishing rates.
 *
 * This group documents library-level neutrino behavior only. Focused M1 unit
 * test sources are shipped under @c Unit_Tests/ and are discovered by
 * @c configure as ordinary @c unit_test_*.c targets, subject to its HDF5
 * filtering. Source and target-selection evidence do not establish test
 * execution, downstream host integration, or external physical validation.
 *
 * The public declarations in @ref ghl_m1.h and
 * @ref ghl_neutrino_rate_provider.h are members of this group. The shared
 * component-wise @ref ghl_calculate_Rusanov_flux belongs to the
 * @ref Flux_Source group; the neutrino face operation uses the M1-specific
 * four-point transport contract described above.
 *
 * Functional API navigation: @ref m1_closure, @ref m1_transport,
 * @ref m1_sources, @ref m1_solver, and @ref m1_rates. Optional diffusion and
 * diagnostic operations are independent facilities; a host integration does
 * not need to call every group in sequence.
 *
 * Source callers may enable final comoving mean-energy bounds through
 * @c ghl_m1_neutrino_parameters::enforce_mean_energy_bounds. Positive bounds
 * reject an out-of-range repaired endpoint, nonpositive bounds disable that
 * side, and @c N == 0 retains the ratio-check skip. The branched source
 * option @c ghl_m1_neutrino_source_options::thermalized_number_threshold uses
 * a negative value to disable equilibrium number projection; zero selects it
 * even for zero opacity or timestep. That projection remains distinct from
 * backward-Euler number integration and @c N_floor repair.
 */

/** @defgroup m1_closure M1 Closure and Moments
 * @ingroup Radiation
 *
 * Closure construction, closure validation diagnostics, comoving moments, and
 * the radiation stress-energy tensor. Decomposition and fallback diagnostics
 * are optional observability APIs.
 */

/** @defgroup m1_transport M1 Transport and Diffusion
 * @ingroup Radiation
 *
 * Face fluxes, transport speeds, four-point blending, and the optional
 * energy-flux diffusion correction. Diffusion is an independent host-selected
 * correction, not a required step in every transport update.
 */

/** @defgroup m1_sources M1 Geometry and Matter Sources
 * @ingroup Radiation
 *
 * Geometric and matter-coupling sources, plus the single-species and paired
 * neutrino source operations. The host chooses which source operations fit its
 * integration schedule.
 */

/** @defgroup m1_solver M1 Solver Interfaces and Diagnostics
 * @ingroup Radiation
 *
 * Generic Newton callbacks and controls, solver diagnostics, closure outcome
 * counters, and neutrino implicit-update diagnostics.
 */

/** @defgroup m1_rates M1 Neutrino Rate Provider
 * @ingroup Radiation
 *
 * Provider context, cache and diagnostics records, with lifecycle and frozen
 * rate-computation operations.
 */
